  "answer": "The study confirmed only 2 of the 5 cases it was asked for, as the goal status says: S10 and S2. S10 is scene 096988dd with the car at its recorded timing and speed and the ego at 1.4x. S2 is scene 023b7fcc with the car 0.5 s earlier at 2x speed and the ego at 0.6x. Every repeat at both settings failed, but with only a few repeats the 90% ranges sit just above the 0.5 bar, so both are confirmed only by a small margin. In both scenes the policy itself caused the crash: it steered left against the route command and hit the side of a car coming up in the next lane. That car was not the one the study retimed, so the ego's speed at hand-off seems to matter more than the retimed car's timing or speed. One other scene failed once and is unconfirmed: 09a95ffa, where the policy did not brake for a slow lead car. No other scene failed, and none of the failures look like simulator artifacts.",
